<title>UK: BGB plans $500 million five-year bond - dealers.</title>
<headline>BGB plans $500 million five-year bond - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bankgesellschaft Berlin (BGB) plans to issue a $500 million five-year Eurobond this week, syndicate managers said on Monday.</p>
<p>The mandate had not yet been awarded, they said.</p>
<p>Spread talk for the deal was around 20 basis points over U.S. Treasury notes, bankers said.</p>
<p>BGB is an active Euromarket borrower, raising funds via its BGB Finance (Ireland) Plc subsidiary.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
